.TH WM-AUTOSTART 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wm-autostart \- start wmmenud and wmnotify with Window Maker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm-autostart install
[\-\-no\-menu] [\-\-no\-notify] [\-\-dry\-run]
.br
.B wm-autostart remove
[\-\-dry\-run]
.br
.B wm-autostart status
.SH DESCRIPTION
Edits Window Maker's autostart script (\fB$WMAKER_USER_ROOT\fR/Library/WindowMaker/autostart, default
~/GNUstep/Library/WindowMaker/autostart). Its lines sit between "# >>> wm-desktop" and "# <<< wm-desktop" markers:
\fBinstall\fR replaces that block, \fBremove\fR deletes only that block, and every other line is left as it was.
The file is backed up to autostart.bak\-\fItime\fR before each change. Dockapps and other entries are not touched.
